-- title:
--   Regular special fibre at ordinary points, q=2 case
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime subject to the hypothesis $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carries $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ by all quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ admitting integral $q$-expansions, $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ being the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with uniformiser $\varpi$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent image the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot jNumQ$ of the modular invariant. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ for some power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Consider the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X} =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel` $A\,K\,j$, the pushout of the two charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$; let $z \in \mathfrak{X}$, let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section pulled back from $\varpi$ along the structure morphism $\mathfrak{X} \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Assume $z$ is the image under the finite-chart immersion of a point $y$ of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the chart algebra $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin` $A\,K\,j$ whose prime $\mathfrak{p}_y$ is maximal, that there is a homomorphism $\varphi : A_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \Omega$ into an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel $\mathfrak{p}_y$ such that $\varphi(j)$ does not lie in `ssJSet` $q\,\Omega$ (the set of $t$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $t$ has trivial $q$-torsion), and that every element of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in the nonunits of $W_0$ lies in $\mathfrak{p}_y$. Let $K_0 \le K$ be the analogous field built from the $\Gamma_0(M')$ $q$-expansion function field, an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, with $j_0 \in K_0$ nonzero having the same Laurent image, and let $\iota : A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K_0, j_0) \to A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the inclusion $K_0 \subseteq K$; assume the structure morphism of the two-chart model of $(K_0, j_0)$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ is smooth. Then, with $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ an $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K_0, j_0)$-algebra via $\iota$: if the extension is unramified at every prime $\mathfrak{Q} \subseteq \mathfrak{p}_y$ of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ of height one, then the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak{X}$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is a purity statement for the normalised full-level (Igusa-type) integral model: regularity of the local ring of the special fibre at a closed point whose $j$-invariant reduces to an ordinary value is deduced from unramifiedness over the smooth $\Gamma_0(M')$ floor at the height-one primes below that point. It is the $q = 2$ case, and feeds the perfect-field form [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isMaximal_of_not_mem_ssJSet_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_twoChartIntegralModel_xH_of_perfectField_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isMaximal_of_not_mem_ssJSet_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_twoChartIntegralModel_xH_of_perfectField_of_eq_two).
